overty we see in the  United States people face very different  challenges you know the biggest being in  in rural Guatemala a lot of people just  don't have access to very very basic  needs like enough food you know a lot of  people were just eating rice and  tortillas every day whereas in the  United States you tend not to see quite  that level of food insecurity a lot of  times people are facing  you know much bigger social issues you  know less access to quality education or  quality work even you know have security  issues with gangs or the neighborhoods  they're living in so these issues that  people are facing are very different and  not to say that of course there isn't  significant food insecurity in the US  but but it's different and and there's  no question that the film does a good  job of kind of pointing that out  last thing in the brief few minutes we  have left here the generosity of the  people that you guys encountered to me  was absolutely  and we're talking like like the subject  of the film is people who are living on  very little money who still went out of  their way seemingly to to feed you guys  and be generous with you guys  absolutely the community in Pena Blanca  was absolutely absolutely incredible and  you know we learned so much from them we  were brought into people's homes they  were so generous with their time and  their energy and we've actually been  back every year since we created the  film we have an update video coming out  about the life of Rosa who I mentioned  earlier before she's incredibly  inspirational which you can check out  our website living on one org and you  know it's a home away from home from us  it's not it's somewhere that we will  always go back to in pretty special  place we've been speaking with Zack and  Rossi as you mentioned the website is  living on one org and the film which I  highly recommend is living on one dollar  Zack thanks so much for coming on today  thanks for having me

